tgs:LinkNote.ChaliceAndBladePower_PowerVersusLife a thinkr:LinkNote,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:aboutObject tgs:Concept.PowerVersusLife ;
    thinkr:aboutSubject tgs:Concept.ChaliceAndBladePower ;
    thinkr:calculatedConfidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:hasEvidence tgs:Evidence.ChaliceAndBladePower_PowerVersusLife_TGS_116 ;
    skos:scopeNote "Eisler-Hagens convergence (added 2026-10-19) on the triple tgs:Concept.ChaliceAndBladePower thinkr:convergesWith tgs:Concept.PowerVersusLife. Both set power over life against life itself as the central contest of the age. Eisler's frame is relational (family, gender, the definition of power); Nate's is energetic (power riding successive surpluses). Frankly_82 comes ten months after TGS_116, and Nate does not cite her there, so no influence is claimed. Stays Candidate until MJSullivan reviews it."@en .

